users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T15:22:29Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T15:22:29Z","body":"I don't think it makes sense to test (de)serialization of all `Variant` types for typed arrays of dictionaries. Even if all `Variant` types are not tested yet (I haven't looked), we should test them separately, not in combination with typed arrays and dictionaries.\r\n\r\nI would just test one `Variant` type and one native type for typed arrays. The same for typed dictionaries, plus cases like `Dictionary[int, Variant]({})` and `Dictionary[Variant, int]({})`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590228949/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2595304465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101429#issuecomment-2595304465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101429","id":2595304465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6asTQR","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T11:45:27Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T11:45:27Z","body":"The PR was mostly inspired by the `*;Resource` dictionary issue in #100889 which slipped by due to not having this test, so I also wanted to check all Variant types to see if they succeeded (which they did). I suppose doing all native Variant types is unnecessary though, since the same collection-typing logic is run for all native Variant types, so I will only do `int` for this (and maybe `Object`). However, I do think `Resource` and `Node` should be included since they are special cases.\r\n\r\nThere are only a few Variant writer/parser tests other than the Arrays and Dictionaries, though I wonder if they should be added in this proposal since it only mentions typed Arrays and Dictionaries. I could always edit the title to implement Variant writer/parser tests in general, though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2595304465/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimize